~ roof_arrival

Unknown: The top of the cathedral. The whole city, all at once, and all of it grey. [ID:CH4_ROOF_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ ridge_city_look

Unknown: Every street I emptied, laid out like a confession. [ID:CH4_RIDGE_CITY_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ belfry_far_look

Unknown: The belfry. He's up there with the book. [ID:CH4_BELFRY_FAR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stone_look

Unknown: A loose block of stone, about as long as I am tall. [ID:CH4_STONE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stone_take

Unknown: Heavy. Shadows are stronger than they look. [ID:CH4_STONE_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ bridge_door_look

Unknown: Back to the covered bridge. [ID:CH4_BRIDGE_DOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ buttress_arrival

Unknown: A flying buttress. Built to hold a cathedral up, not a shadow. [ID:CH4_BUTTRESS_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ buttress_gap_look

Unknown: A slab's fallen out. The fog below goes on a long way. [ID:CH4_BUTTRESS_GAP_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ buttress_gap_blocked

Unknown: I'm not jumping that. Something to fill the gap, though. [ID:CH4_BUTTRESS_GAP_BLOCKED_1]

=> END

~ buttress_gap_bridged

Unknown: The stone fits. Cathedrals were built a block at a time. So, apparently, are apologies. [ID:CH4_BUTTRESS_GAP_BRIDGED_1]

=> END

~ cathedral_wall_look

Unknown: The cathedral's flank, windows taller than houses. [ID:CH4_WALL_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ gallery_arrival

Unknown: Gargoyles. A gallery of critics. [ID:CH4_GALLERY_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ gargoyles_look

Unknown: Faces carved to frighten off the dark. They're not doing well tonight. [ID:CH4_GARGOYLES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ key_gargoyle_look

Unknown: That one has a key in its mouth. Someone hid it where only a bird could reach. [ID:CH4_KEY_GARGOYLE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ key_gargoyle_take

Unknown: Sorry. I need that more than you do. [ID:CH4_KEY_GARGOYLE_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ key_gargoyle_empty

Unknown: Its jaws are empty now. It looks almost relieved. [ID:CH4_KEY_GARGOYLE_EMPTY_1]

=> END

~ dovecote_arrival

Unknown: A dovecote, on top of the world. Grey doves. And one white. [ID:CH4_DOVECOTE_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ doves_look

Unknown: Grey doves, all asleep. And one white one, awake, watching me. [ID:CH4_DOVES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ dovecote_door_look

Unknown: The dovecote door. Locked, from the outside. [ID:CH4_DOVECOTE_DOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ dovecote_door_open

Unknown: The key turns. Someone comes out. [ID:CH4_DOVECOTE_DOOR_OPEN_1]

=> END

~ trapdoor4_look

Unknown: A trapdoor, down into an attic. [ID:CH4_TRAPDOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ trapdoor4_locked

Unknown: That's someone's home. I'm not walking into it uninvited. Not this time. [ID:CH4_TRAPDOOR_LOCKED_1]

=> END

~ tower_door4_look

Unknown: The door into the tower. And up. [ID:CH4_TOWER_DOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ tower_door4_locked

Unknown: Not yet. There's something I have to say first, and somebody I have to say it to. [ID:CH4_TOWER_DOOR_LOCKED_1]

=> END

~ dove_look

Unknown: A woman in a veil, with a white dove on her hand. There's colour in that veil. Just a little. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ dove_talk

if GameState.get_flag("dove_forgave")
	Dove: Go on. He's waiting. And then come back to me. [ID:CH4_DOVE_AFTER_1]
	=> END
if not GameState.get_flag("dove_met")
	do GameState.set_flag("dove_met")
	Dove: There you are. [ID:CH4_DOVE_MEET_1]
	Unknown: You know me. [ID:CH4_DOVE_MEET_2]
	Dove: I'd know you in the dark. I've had a lot of practice. [ID:CH4_DOVE_MEET_3]
	Dove: You took my name, Ulric. You didn't take you. I kept you. Somebody had to. [ID:CH4_DOVE_MEET_4]
=> dove_ask

~ dove_ask

Dove: Well? [ID:CH4_DOVE_ASK]
- Why did you forgive me? [ID:CH4_DOVE_ASK_WHY]
	Dove: I didn't, for a long time. I sat up here hating you, with no name to sign it with. [ID:CH4_DOVE_WHY_1]
	Dove: Then I found I couldn't hate a man who'd made himself so small. You were so frightened, at the end. [ID:CH4_DOVE_WHY_2]
	=> dove_ask
- The Registrar has the book. [ID:CH4_DOVE_ASK_BOOK]
	Dove: I know. I heard him on the stair, muttering like a pen on paper. [ID:CH4_DOVE_BOOK_1]
	Dove: You could take it from him. You were always good at taking things. [ID:CH4_DOVE_BOOK_2]
	Dove: Or you could give something, for once. [ID:CH4_DOVE_BOOK_3]
	=> dove_ask
- May I see your room? [if not GameState.get_flag("dove_room_ok") /] [ID:CH4_DOVE_ASK_ROOM]
	do GameState.set_flag("dove_room_ok")
	Dove: You may. Don't touch the hymn book. [ID:CH4_DOVE_ROOM_1]
	Dove: There's a letter on the desk. You wrote it. You never sent it. You should read it before you do anything brave. [ID:CH4_DOVE_ROOM_2]
	=> dove_ask
- Goodbye. [ID:CH4_DOVE_ASK_BYE]
	Dove: Don't say that. You always said that. [ID:CH4_DOVE_BYE]
	=> END

~ dove_letter

Unknown: I wrote this. I couldn't say it then. I'll say it now. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_1]
Unknown: I'm sorry. For your name, and for every name. I was afraid of a city that remembered, so I made one that couldn't. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_2]
Dove: ... [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_3]
Dove: You finally said it to my face. Even if you haven't got one. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_4]
Dove: Here. I kept this for you, the night they broke your stone. The Gravedigger put moss over it, and I put it in my heart. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_5]
Dove: The U. The beginning of you. It's enough to start from. Now go and give them back theirs. [ID:CH4_DOVE_LETTER_6]

=> END

~ dove_other

Dove: That's not what I'm waiting for. [ID:CH4_DOVE_OTHER_1]

=> END

~ dove_room_arrival

Unknown: Her room. Small, careful, and full of the things she refused to forget. [ID:CH4_DOVE_ROOM_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ banner_look

Unknown: The choir's banner. Blue. Real blue. The only colour I've seen in this city that wasn't a memory. [ID:CH4_BANNER_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ keepsakes_look

Unknown: A hymn book, a white feather, a little carved dove. A whole life, on one shelf. [ID:CH4_KEEPSAKES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ bed_look

Unknown: A narrow bed. She slept up here, alone, keeping watch over a city that forgot her. [ID:CH4_BED_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ desk4_look

Unknown: A writing desk, and a folded letter. [ID:CH4_DESK_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ desk4_take

Unknown: My handwriting. I'll take it. It's mine to deliver. [ID:CH4_DESK_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ desk4_empty

Unknown: The desk is bare. The letter is where it should have been years ago. [ID:CH4_DESK_EMPTY_1]

=> END

~ ladder4_look

Unknown: Back up to the dovecote. [ID:CH4_LADDER_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ letter_text_look

Unknown: "Elise. I can't undo it. I'm sorry. I was afraid of a city that remembered." [ID:CH4_LETTER_TEXT_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ letter_sign_look

Unknown: Signed with a single U. Of course. [ID:CH4_LETTER_SIGN_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ ledge_arrival

Unknown: Behind the rose window. The nave far below, where I first saw the past. [ID:CH4_LEDGE_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ rose_look

Unknown: The rose window, from behind. The moon fills in the missing glass. [ID:CH4_ROSE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ rose_use

Unknown: The lead's still warm, where the sun used to come through. [ID:CH4_ROSE_USE_1]

=> END

~ song_return

Unknown: The whole cathedral full. And her voice, above all of them, singing the names. Every name I'd taken, one after another. [ID:CH4_SONG_RETURN_1]
Unknown: And me, in the doorway, with my book. I walk up the aisle. Everyone watches. [ID:CH4_SONG_RETURN_2]
Unknown: And I take her name in front of all of them, so they'll know what singing costs. [ID:CH4_SONG_RETURN_3]
Unknown: Elise. Her name was Elise. [ID:CH4_SONG_RETURN_4]

=> END

~ nave_below_look

Unknown: The nave, far below. The saint's statue, the altar. Where all this started, for me. [ID:CH4_NAVE_BELOW_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ ledge_door_look

Unknown: Back out to the roof. [ID:CH4_LEDGE_DOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stair_door_look

Unknown: A door to the bell stair. [ID:CH4_STAIR_DOOR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stair_arrival4

Unknown: The bell stair. Ropes, hanging still. Something's waiting at the top. [ID:CH4_STAIR_ARRIVAL_1]

=> END

~ ropes4_look

Unknown: Bell ropes, thick as my arm. Nobody's rung them since I died. [ID:CH4_ROPES_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stair_up_look4

Unknown: Up. [ID:CH4_STAIR_UP_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ stair_down_look4

Unknown: Back down. [ID:CH4_STAIR_DOWN_LOOK_1]

=> END
